{"id":1585,"date":"2020-12-02T13:12:29","date_gmt":"2020-12-02T21:12:29","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1585"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:38:34","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:38:34","slug":"codrone-blockly-jr-leds","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-blockly-jr-leds\/","title":{"rendered":"LEDs"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215450b408\" name=\"6a2215450b408\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What is an LED?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">LED stands for \u201clight-emitting diode\u201d. A <\/span><b>diode <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">is an electronic device that allows an electronic current to flow in only one direction. LEDs are beginning to replace traditional light bulbs because they are more efficient.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Your CoDrone has 6 <\/span><b>RGB <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">LEDs: one on each of the four arms, one for the eyes, and one for the tail. RGB stands for red, green, and blue. Using the three colors, you can create almost every color imaginable! Aside from making your drone look cool, LEDs provide another form of feedback. For example, the tail light can tell you the connection status of your drone. A solid green tail light means your drone is connected, while the fl<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">ashing green light indicates it\u2019s in pairing mode. While you cannot change the colors of this particular LED, the remaining 5 LEDs can be programmed to produce any color and pattern that you want!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215450b5ac\" name=\"6a2215450b5ac\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Parameters<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">CoDrone provides functionality so that you can either change the arm LEDs, eye LEDs, or both at the same<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400\">time! All of these functions can be found in the Lights menu.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Each LED block has one or more of these parameters:<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Color &#8211; <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">To change the color of the LEDs, click on the color. It will bring up a menu so that you can choose which color you want to change your CoDrone LEDs to.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong>Brightness &#8211;<\/strong> In the solid LED blocks, <span style=\"font-weight: 400\">this refers to the<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400\">light&#8217;s brightness, with 0 being off and 100 being full brightness. <\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Mode &#8211; <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">The mode refers to the light pattern that you want to choose:<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">BLINK fl<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">ashes LEDs on and off<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">DOUBLE BLINK<\/span> fl<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">ashes LEDs on twice before turning off<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">DIMMING <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">fades the LEDs in and out<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Interval &#8211; <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">T<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">he frequency<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400\">(per second) for any light pattern. The interval value will never be negative!<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1586&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215450b617\" name=\"6a2215450b617\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>LED rainbow<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Pair to CoDrone and practice using the LEDs to make a rainbow. Make sure each color shows for one second before switching to the next color. For optimal brightness, set the brightness to 100. Use the wait block for one second in between the color blocks so you can see each color before it moves on to the next one. Have the pattern repeat forever using a loop!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1588&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215450b67a\" name=\"6a2215450b67a\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">The first system of electrical telecommunication was the telegraph. It was a device that sent pulses of electricity, either long or short, to send messages. Letters were defined by unique combinations of long and short beeps, called Morse Code. You may be able to recognize this message:\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>. . . _ _ _ . . .\u00a0<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">This message reads SOS! <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Look up the <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Morse_code#\/media\/File:International_Morse_Code.svg\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Morse Code alphabet <\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">and learn some letters. Try coming up with a method to send messages using Morse Code with your CoDrone. If you want, pair up to decode each other\u2019s messages. <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Use long and short flashes to send your messages using different values for the wait block.\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 5 What is an LED? [vc_column_text]LED stands for \u201clight-emitting diode\u201d. A diode is an electronic device that allows an electronic current to flow in only one direction. LEDs&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-blockly-jr-leds\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1754,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":806,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1817,1763,1777,1793,626,1533,1438,853,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2135,2108,2164,2120,2122],"class_list":["post-1585","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-led","lesson-tag-programming","module-junior","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1585","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":4,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1585\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":2462,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1585\/revisions\/2462"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1754"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1585"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1585"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1585"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}